        en: 'Six tiny commands written by six people who never met, chained in one line, turn a gigabyte log into a report. At the same moment your browser asks a server on another continent for an appointment that lives in a database you never see. Two architecture families solve two different problems: data flowing through independent transforms, and one shared truth across machines. Today you learn when to pick each — and exactly what it costs.',
